# Emerging Digital Optical Disc Technologies: An Opportunity and a Challenge for Educational Researchers.

**Authors:** Harvey, Francis A.

## Abstract
Description of new applications of digital optical disc storage technologies focuses on CD-ROM (Compact Disc--Read Only Memory); CD-I (Compact Disc--Interactive); and DV-I (Digital Video--Interactive). Features of each technology are described in the context of instructional design and educational technology, and the role of educational research in their development is discussed. (LRW)

